Adapted sources (this round):

1. dsh-web-mobile (MIT, https://github.com/mexiaosqwq/dsh-web-mobile, Copyright (c) 2026
   mexiaosqwq) — the current NOTICE adapts code from this project at the
   versions listed below; the upstream file layout has evolved (v1.5.0 moved
   the overlay interactions out of `src/client/MobileNavOverlay.tsx` into
   `src/client/effects/phone-chrome.ts`), so the mappings below describe the
   upstream source the fragments were adapted from at adaptation time:
   - src/client/styles/layout.css.ts  → adapted into
     src/client/mobile/mobile.css.ts (drawer, conversation text, composer
     row, settings dialog sheet rules, and — R13/v0.2.1 — the active-phase
     header-yielding + always-visible sidebar entry placement rules)
   - src/client/styles/misc.css.ts    → adapted into the tablet/wide-mobile
     sheet-cap and desktop-guard media queries in the same file
   - src/client/effects/phone-chrome.ts → adapted into
     src/client/mobile/index.ts (viewport-fit + theme-color + gesturestart)
   - src/client/MobileNavOverlay.tsx  → adapted into
     src/client/mobile/MobileOverlay.tsx (frame marker, backdrop, floating
     open button, drawer close-on-navigate; upstream v1.5.0 removed this
     file and moved the same interactions into effects/phone-chrome.ts)
   - R13/v0.2.1 addition: the upstream v1.5.0 MobileNavToggle design idea
     (an always-available sidebar entry for active conversations bound to
     `ctx.layout.toggleSidebar()`, coexisting with the session-header
     crumbs) was re-implemented inside src/client/mobile/MobileOverlay.tsx
     + mobile.css.ts rather than copied as a header-slot component.
   Adapted fragments keep the original structure where practical; the marker
   attribute was renamed to `data-dsh-remote-mobile` and unrelated plugin
   compat (aionui / git graph / stats) was deliberately excluded.

2. DeepSeek Harness (MIT, https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness)
   - packages/client/tsdown.client.ts  → the plugin's tsdown.config.ts
     mirrors the client-bundle preset (loader handoff, externals, purity
     gate, CSS handling) for an out-of-tree package
   - R14/v0.2.1: packages/host/directory-picker-browse/src/index.ts (the
     official browse directory-picker backend) → the read-only directory
     listing semantics in src/workspace-browse.ts (opendir streaming into a
     name-sorted bounded window with a `truncated` flag, symlink
     enterability probes, breadcrumb ancestry, POSIX dot-prefix hidden
     flags, the fully-qualified path fence, and abort-aware file reads).
     Only the `list` primitive is adapted; create/delete/modify are
     deliberately absent. The mobile client surface
     (src/client/workspace-browse/MobileDirectoryFlow.tsx) mirrors the
     official ui-directory-picker-browse semantics (initial level = Host
     home, Home crumb inside the home subtree, selection = current level)
     without depending on the official packages at runtime.
   - Design tokens and the Button primitive are used as-is from the DSH
     installation at runtime (no code copied).

